\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Eternal Power ! whose high abode
\par Becomes the grandeur of a God :
\par Infinite lengths beyond the bounds
\par Where stars revolve their little rounds.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thee while the first archangel! Sings,
\par He hides his face beneath his wings,
\par And throngs of shinning thrones around
\par Fall worshipping, and spread the ground.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Lord, what shall earth and ashes do?
\par We would adore our Maker too;
\par From sin and dust to Thee we cry,
\par The Great, the Holy, and the high !
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Earth from afar has heard Thy fame,
\par And babes have learnt to lisp Thy name:
\par But O the glories of Thy mind 
\par Leave all our soaring thoughts behind !
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. God is in Heaven, and men below;
\par Be short our tunes, our words be few;
\par A sacred reverence checks our songs,
\par And praise sits silent on our tongues.
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

